  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved national social protection system in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s National Strategy for Transformation (NST1) highlights the central role of social protection in poverty reduction and improving the standard of living for all citizens. The &quot;Reinforcing Social Security System and Implementation of National Policies&quot; initiative aims to enhance Rwanda&apos;s social protection system, with a particular focus on expanding coverage for informal workers and strengthening the linkages between social protection and employment.

The project supports the Government of Rwanda in strengthening both contributory and non-contributory social protection schemes, such as the Rwanda Social Security Board&apos;s (RSSB) pension and health schemes, and the national social assistance program (VUP) for vulnerable households. Despite significant progress, coverage remains limited, with contributory schemes reaching less than 10% of the population. The COVID-19 pandemic further underscored the vulnerability of workers, particularly those in informal employment, which constitutes 87% of the workforce.</narrative>
  </description>
